  "term": "cerebral contusion",
  "definition": "Cerebral contusion is a traumatic brain injury in which the brain has been injured severely enough to place the person at risk of rapid worsening. It is associated with a higher risk of death, and outcome is often assessed in relation to survival and level of consciousness.",
